    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1026">

                <pb facs="0779" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/3279</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Dawson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-07T18:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 6, 6 p.m. Approximately 90 Americans in Chamal Colony, fully advised of
                    conditions and warned various times to withdraw from Mexico, decided to remain,
                    preferring to take chances rather than abandon their only property. Believe it
                    useless to warn them again. I am reliably informed many late refugees are
                    already returning in belief that crisis is passed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
